From 28e50a7217b1c81fd38143179e6d5f9f9b3ca5f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qualcomm-toolbox <169756160+qcom-toolbox@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 15:21:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] umi: ADSP apps_mem, heap pageslen, LPASS core votes; AFE port
 side still silent

apps_mem request_map64 is answered with low RAM after the remote heap,
mapped into the ADSP with FastRPC mmap (method 2, the downstream 64-bit
call; method 4 got -1, 0218) and hyp-assigned for remote-heap requests.
createstaticpd now passes the heap with pageslen 1 as the downstream driver
does; then the audio PD no longer asks apps_mem at all.

Before the clock the AFE gets the LPASS core hardware votes (blocks 3 and 4),
the first AFE commands it ever answered (0x100f5, handles 0x1b / 0x1c). Port
and service commands are still not answered, whatever their size: a 24-byte
DEVICE_STOP and the 68-byte I2S config alike (hex-dumped, byte-exact against
the downstream structs). The clock set alternates SVC_SET_PARAM and
SVC_SET_PARAM_V2. Test boot-arg sweetadspnocirrus=1 hides the speaker
protection module from the audio PD's loader; module freads are logged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 bsd/dev/sweet_adsp.c | 224 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--------
 bsd/dev/sweet_slpi.c |  25 ++++-
